# End-of-Session Sync

> **When to invoke**: At the end of a productive session, or when the user
> says "sync", "end-of-session sync", or "session cleanup".
>
> **Project context**: Read the current project's `.cursor/rules/project-namespace.mdc`
> for project name, neural-memory tags, verify commands, and GitNexus repo name.
>
> **Ordering rule** (harness-mcp-bridge Phase 3 / ADR-0001 SSOT): docs first →
> memory-bank index → nmem_remember → GitNexus refresh → cross-check →
> interactive_feedback.

---

## Session-Type Skip Matrix

Not every step applies to every session. Determine the session type first:

| Step | Code + Docs | Code-Only | Docs-Only | Setup/Config |
|------|:-----------:|:---------:|:---------:|:------------:|
| 0 Gather Context | FULL | FULL | REQUIRED only | FULL |
| 1 Reflection | ALL items | Skip product truth | Skip validation | Skip validation |
| 1.5 Doc Completeness | ALL | ALL | SKIP | SKIP |
| 2 Harness Docs | ALL | Skip product docs | ALL | ALL |
| 3 Memory-Bank | ALL | ALL | ALL | ALL |
| 4 Serena Memories | ALL | ALL | SKIP | ALL |
| 5 Neural Memory | ALL | ALL | ALL | ALL |
| 6 GitNexus Re-index | YES | YES | SKIP | SKIP |
| 7 Cross-Check | ALL | ALL | ALL | ALL |
| 8 Summary + Confirm | ALL | ALL | ALL | ALL |

---

## Step 0 — Gather Context (read-only, parallel)

Before updating anything, read the current state. Skip files that do not
exist in the current project. Parallel execution of reads is the goal but
sequential is acceptable (e.g., on Windows/PowerShell where MCP calls
serialize).

**First**: Read `.cursor/rules/project-namespace.mdc` to extract `project_tag`,
`gitnexus_repo_name`, and verify commands for later steps.

### Required reads (always)
```
nmem_recap(level=2, compact=true, token_budget=800)
Read .cursor/rules/project-namespace.mdc   # MUST — project identity
Read memory-bank/activeContext.md           # if present
Read memory-bank/progress.md               # if present
Read docs/TEST_MATRIX.md                   # if present
Read docs/HARNESS_BACKLOG.md               # if present
Read docs/stories/backlog.md               # if present
```

### Optional reads (when reflection checklist demands them)
```
Read memory-bank/decisionLog.md            # if new ADRs were created
Read memory-bank/systemPatterns.md         # if architecture changed
Read memory-bank/techContext.md            # if stack/deps changed
Read memory-bank/productContext.md         # if scope/goals changed
Read memory-bank/projectbrief.md           # rarely — only if core reqs changed
Read docs/product/*                        # if product truth may have changed
Read .serena/memories/project_overview.md  # if present
Read .serena/memories/style_and_conventions.md
Read .serena/memories/suggested_commands.md
Read .serena/memories/task_completion_checklist.md
```

---

## Step 1 — Reflection Checklist (Phase 3.4 from harness-mcp-bridge)

Answer each question. Any "yes" drives an update in Steps 2–5.

- [ ] Did **product truth** change? → update `docs/product/*`
- [ ] Did **validation expectations** change? → update `docs/TEST_MATRIX.md`
- [ ] Did **architecture rules** change? → update `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`
      (if present) or `memory-bank/systemPatterns.md` + new ADR in
      `docs/decisions/`
- [ ] Did we discover a **repeated failure pattern**? → log in
      `docs/HARNESS_BACKLOG.md` or `nmem_remember(type=error)`
- [ ] Did the **next agent need a clearer instruction**? → update the
      relevant `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` or `docs/HARNESS.md`
- [ ] Were there **new design decisions**? → 3-step write (ADR + index +
      nmem_remember)
- [ ] Were **Known Issues resolved**? → remove from activeContext.md and
      progress.md (if those files exist)
- [ ] Were **new stories started or completed**? → update `docs/stories/*`
      status and `docs/stories/backlog.md` (if present)

---

## Step 1.5 — Harness Document Completeness Check

Before updating existing docs, verify that all required harness documents
exist for work completed this session. Missing documents are a common gap
when implementation moves faster than documentation.

### Check for each completed/in-progress story (US-NNN):

```
# For each story identified in Step 1 reflection:
Glob docs/stories/US-NNN*       # story file or directory exists?
```

**If the story has a high-risk lane**, verify the full story pack exists:

| Required file | Purpose |
|---------------|---------|
| `docs/stories/US-NNN-<slug>/overview.md` | Current vs target behavior, affected users |
| `docs/stories/US-NNN-<slug>/design.md` | Architecture, IPC contracts, key decisions |
| `docs/stories/US-NNN-<slug>/execplan.md` | Step-by-step execution plan with status |
| `docs/stories/US-NNN-<slug>/validation.md` | Unit/integration/E2E proof status |

**If the story has a normal lane**, at minimum:

| Required file | Purpose |
|---------------|---------|
| `docs/stories/US-NNN-<slug>.md` | Single-file story (overview + plan) |

### Check for each design decision made this session:

```
Glob docs/decisions/NNNN-*.md   # ADR file exists?
```

If an ADR was made but no file exists, create it from `docs/templates/decision.md`.

### Check for product truth changes:

If product capabilities changed (new features, new contracts, new limits):

```
Glob docs/product/*             # relevant product doc exists?
```

If the feature has no product doc and it introduces user-visible behavior,
create one in `docs/product/<feature>.md`.

### Check for backlog entry:

```
Read docs/stories/backlog.md    # new story listed?
```

If a new story was completed but not listed in the backlog, add it.

### Check for TEST_MATRIX row:

```
Read docs/TEST_MATRIX.md        # new story has a row?
```

If the story has no row in the test matrix, add one with current proof status.

### Action

Create any missing files BEFORE proceeding to Step 2. Use templates from
`docs/templates/` when available. This ensures Step 2 updates existing files
rather than discovering gaps mid-sync.

