## Step 2 — Update Harness Docs (SSOT layer — update first)

These are the source of truth. Update before memory-bank indexes.

| File | Update when... |
|---|---|
| `docs/product/*` | Product contracts changed |
| `docs/stories/*` + `backlog.md` | Story status changed (started, blocked, done) |
| `docs/TEST_MATRIX.md` | Validation expectations or proof status changed |
| `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` or `memory-bank/systemPatterns.md` | Architecture rules changed |
| `docs/decisions/NNNN-*.md` | New architectural decision made (from template) |
| `docs/HARNESS_BACKLOG.md` | Structural gap or friction discovered |

---

## Step 3 — Update Memory-Bank (index layer — reflects docs)

Read each file that exists in the current project, compare with actual
codebase state, update stale content:

| File | What to check |
|---|---|
| `activeContext.md` | Current Focus matches reality. Remove resolved Known Issues. Update "What Was Just Completed" and "Next Steps". Update Active Stories table. |
| `progress.md` | Move completed items from "Not Yet" to "Completed". Remove fixed Known Issues. Update current status. |
| `decisionLog.md` | Add row to the ADR index table for any new ADR created in Step 2. |
| `systemPatterns.md` | Add new patterns/architecture. Update changed patterns. |
| `techContext.md` | Update if stack, config, dependencies, or conventions changed. |
| `productContext.md` | Only update if scope or goals changed. |
| `projectbrief.md` | Only update if core requirements changed. |

---

## Step 4 — Update Serena Memories

Read `.serena/memories/*` (if present), update to match current codebase:

| File | What to check |
|---|---|
| `project_overview.md` | New files, classes, services added. Removed items. |
| `style_and_conventions.md` | New patterns or convention changes. |
| `suggested_commands.md` | New build/test commands or changed paths. |
| `task_completion_checklist.md` | Updated completion criteria. |

