## Step 5 — Persist to Neural Memory

> **No MCP layer available** (e.g. a plain Claude Code CLI session with no
> `nmem_*` tools bound): skip the calls below and instead append the
> session summary as a bullet under `memory-bank/activeContext.md` →
> "Recent Changes" (and, if the friction is structural, a
> `docs/HARNESS_BACKLOG.md` item). Note explicitly in the Step 8 summary
> that cross-session Neural Memory persistence was degraded this session.

Store session knowledge for cross-session recall.
**Use the project tag extracted from `project-namespace.mdc` in Step 0**
(e.g. `tags: ["dcmvn_cs", "<area>"]`).

```
# For each design decision made this session:
nmem_remember(
  content="ADR-NNNN: <title>. File: docs/decisions/NNNN-...md",
  type="decision",
  tags=["<project_tag>", "<area>"],   # e.g. ["pydcmvn-extension", "harness"]
  priority=7
)

# For each bug fix or error encountered:
nmem_remember(
  content="ERROR: <what happened>. ROOT CAUSE: <why>. FIX: <what fixed it>.",
  type="error",
  tags=["<project_tag>", "<module>"],  # e.g. ["pydcmvn-extension", "validate"]
  priority=7
)

# For each new pattern or insight discovered:
nmem_remember(
  content="INSIGHT: <what was learned>. CONTEXT: <when this applies>.",
  type="insight",
  tags=["<project_tag>", "<area>"],    # e.g. ["pydcmvn-extension", "architecture"]
  priority=6
)

# LAST — session summary (always call, even if nothing else was stored):
nmem_auto(action="process", text="<brief session summary>")
```

