## Step 6 — GitNexus Re-index (MANDATORY for code-change sessions)

Skip this step ONLY if the session was docs-only or setup/config-only (no
`.cs`, `.js`, `.jsx`, `.ts`, `.tsx`, `.py` source files changed). Otherwise,
**always run** the re-index to keep the code knowledge graph fresh.

### 6.1 — Re-analyze the repo

**Option A — CLI (when `npx gitnexus` is available):**

```bash
npx gitnexus analyze
```

**Option B — MCP (when GitNexus is available as MCP server only):**

```
CallMcpTool server="user-gitnexus" toolName="analyze"
  args={ "repo": "<gitnexus_repo_name>" }
```

This regenerates the symbol graph (`.gitnexus/` directory). Check the
output for the updated node/edge counts. Use `--force` (CLI) or
`"force": true` (MCP) only when the index appears corrupted or out-of-sync.
If the index previously had embeddings (`stats.embeddings > 0` in
`.gitnexus/meta.json`), add `--embeddings` (CLI) or `"embeddings": true` (MCP).

### 6.2 — Refresh bridge data (if bridge script exists)

Use the GitNexus repo name from `project-namespace.mdc` (extracted in Step 0).
**Skip this step entirely if the bridge script does not exist.** Check first:

```bash
# Only run if the bridge script is present
if [ -f .cursor/skills/.global/gitnexus/gitnexus_bridge.py ]; then
  python .cursor/skills/.global/gitnexus/gitnexus_bridge.py --repo <gitnexus_repo_name>
fi
```

Verify `memory-bank/codebaseGraph.md` and
`memory-bank/codebase_graph_summary.json` are updated (if those files exist).

### 6.3 — Verify freshness

After re-index, read `gitnexus://repo/<gitnexus_repo_name>/context` (MCP
resource) or check `.gitnexus/meta.json` timestamp, and confirm the
`lastAnalyzed` timestamp is from this session.

---

## Step 7 — Cross-Check Verification

After all updates, verify consistency:

- [ ] `progress.md` and `activeContext.md` describe the same state (if both exist)
- [ ] `decisionLog.md` has entries for all ADRs in `docs/decisions/`
- [ ] Serena memories and memory-bank describe the same codebase structure
- [ ] No resolved Known Issues remain in activeContext or progress
- [ ] Story statuses in `activeContext.md` match `docs/stories/backlog.md` (if present)
- [ ] `docs/TEST_MATRIX.md` reflects current validation reality

---

## Step 8 — Summary + Confirm

Ensure `nmem_auto(action="process")` was called in Step 5 (it must be the
last persistence action before this summary).

Write a summary of what was synced and call interactive_feedback
(Cursor only — requires the `user-mcp-feedback-enhanced` MCP server):

```
CallMcpTool server="user-mcp-feedback-enhanced" toolName="interactive_feedback"
  args={
    "project_directory": "<project_root>",
    "summary": "<what was updated, what was skipped, any blockers>",
    "timeout": 36000
  }
```

> **No MCP layer available**: do not fabricate this call. End the session
> with a plain written summary to the user instead, explicitly stating
> that `interactive_feedback` and Neural Memory persistence (Step 5) were
> unavailable this session and what was done in their place.
